{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מטה זבולן", :translit "matteh zevulun", :gloss "the tribe of Zebulun"} {:he "ולא אמר ומטה כדרך שאומר באחרים", :translit "ve-lo amar u-matteh ke-derekh she-omer ba-acherim", :gloss "and it does not say 'and the tribe' as it says regarding the others"} {:he "לפי שזבולן היה מפרנס ליששכר", :translit "le-fi she-zevulun hayah mefarnez le-yissakhar", :gloss "because Zebulun supported Issachar"} {:he "וראיתי בתנחומא", :translit "ve-ra'iti be-tanchuma", :gloss "and I saw in the Tanchuma"} {:he "שלא אמר ומטה בזבולון כמו שאמר בכולן", :translit "she-lo amar u-matteh be-zevulun ke-mo she-amar ba-kulan", :gloss "that it does not say 'and the tribe' regarding Zebulun as it said regarding all of them"} {:he "ללמדך שהיה זבולן עוסק בפרקמטיא ונותן לתוך פיו של יששכר", :translit "le-lamedekha she-hayah zevulun osek be-farkematia ve-noten le-tokh piv shel yissakhar", :gloss "to teach you that Zebulun engaged in commerce and placed into the mouth of Issachar"} {:he "לפיכך לא רצה הכתוב לעשותו טפילה לו", :translit "le-fikhakh lo ratzah ha-katuv la'asoto tefilah lo", :gloss "therefore Scripture did not wish to make him subordinate to him"} {:he "לומר ששכרו גדול כמותו", :translit "le-imar she-sakharo gadol ke-moto", :gloss "to say that his reward is great as his"} {:he "עץ חיים היא למחזיקים בה ותומכיה מאושר", :translit "etz chayim hi la-machazikim bah u-tomecheha me'ushar", :gloss "a tree of life she is to those who hold her and her supporters are happy"} {:he "כי בצל החכמה בצל הכסף", :translit "ki be-tzel ha-chokhmah be-tzel ha-kesef", :gloss "for in the shadow of wisdom in the shadow of money"} {:he "לכן חשוב הכל כמטה אחד", :translit "lachen chashuv ha-kol ke-matteh echad", :gloss "therefore all are reckoned as one tribe"} {:he "וכאילו אמר יששכר מטה זבולן", :translit "u-ke-ilu amar yissakhar matteh zevulun", :gloss "and as if it said Issachar the tribe of Zebulun"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note " lexical anomaly: omitting the conjunction 'and' before 'matteh' elevates Zebulun's status"} {:kind :other, :note " inter-textual linkage: Proverbs 3:18 'her supporters' read as Zebulun supporting Issachar's Torah"} {:kind :other, :note " inter-textual linkage: Ecclesiastes 7:12 equates the 'shadow of wisdom' with the 'shadow of money'"}], :frame {:text "The partnership between Zebulun and Issachar — one tribe supporting the other's Torah study financially and sharing the reward — is a recurring rabbinic theme. Genesis Rabbah 72:5 and Genesis Rabbah 99:9 discuss Zebulun engaging in trade while Issachar studies Torah, based on the blessing of Moses in Deuteronomy 33:18 where both tribes are mentioned together. The Tanchuma cited here by Ba'al HaTurim spells out that Scripture avoids subordinating Zebulun to Issachar in this very verse so as to signal equal reward. Proverbs 3:18 ('her supporters are happy') is applied by Berakhot 63a to those who financially support Torah scholars. Ecclesiastes 7:12 ('for in the shadow of wisdom, in the shadow of money') is read midrashically in sources such as the Tanchuma as equating the merit of the one who funds Torah with the one who studies.", :sources ["Genesis Rabbah 72:5" "Genesis Rabbah 99:9" "Deuteronomy 33:18" "Tanchuma Vayechi" "Berakhot 63a" "Proverbs 3:18" "Ecclesiastes 7:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note " lexical anomaly: omitting the conjunction 'and' before 'matteh' elevates Zebulun's status", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note " inter-textual linkage: Proverbs 3:18 'her supporters' read as Zebulun supporting Issachar's Torah", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note " inter-textual linkage: Ecclesiastes 7:12 equates the 'shadow of wisdom' with the 'shadow of money'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:59.241688174Z", :model "glm-5.2"}